  nonce: fef6  # fef6
  message: "PREMISE CHECK 2026-09-30 (dev 134a06d505): CURRENT. Both defects stand as filed.\n\n- (1) docs/adr/0048-*.md:60 still reads \"Both estimators give 44/112 = 39.3%.\" The only commit to the file is d181602ff7 (2026-08-28), and grep finds no 38/112 or 33.9 anywhere in the ADR. 0006 publishes 33.9% (0006 lines 57 and 96), as does README index row 58.\n- (2) ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/measurement_0006_08252026/ledger-final.json is unchanged (mtime Aug 25). Its keys are ['final', 'provenance'], with final = 112 labels, Counter TP 44 / FP 68, and no `refuted` field. pass4-summary.json says refuted = 7 (ArkLib#0, ArkLib#1, guacamole-client#4, jaeger#0, rabbitmq#5, tmux#3, tmux#6), contested = tmux#6, headline_uncontested_tp = 38. That is the item's arithmetic exactly.\n- Since filing, the trap is documented in-repo: measurement 0010 lines 264-270 (54a62e8b08) and 0006 line 220 (d75c034ba9, derive.py reads both files). Per the row's own argument, that is a docstring-class note and does not fix the filename.\n- Cost of fix (2) that the row does not state: five notebook scripts open the file by name (measurement_0006_08252026/final.py and tables.py, gibom_08272026/derive.py, step3_adjudication_08302026/retro.py, measurement_0012_09022026/final.py), and two in-repo records cite the name (0006:220, 0010:233/264). A rename breaks them unless they are updated; adding a `refuted` field does not. The artifact lives OUTSIDE the repo (lab notebook), so part (2) is not a PR change."  # fef6
